## Third-party components

`third-party/` contains source snapshots adapted from upstream projects. They are
NOT covered by the MIT license above; each directory keeps its own license text and
`third-party/PROVENANCE.md` records the upstream project, version, license and every
modification:

- `third-party/cetz/` — adapted from cetz-package/cetz v0.5.2, **LGPL-3.0** (see `third-party/cetz/LICENSE`).
- `third-party/fletcher/` — adapted from Jollywatt/typst-fletcher v0.5.8, **MIT**
  (Copyright (c) 2023 Joseph Wilson, see `third-party/fletcher/LICENSE`).

The example chapters under `chapter/` `#include` these snapshots. Deleting `third-party/`
and those include sites removes the third-party code entirely; the core template in
`njust-thesis/` does not import it.
